--- !u!114 &214206417
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 214206415}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4bda29742d2f3f54e9e8117d9f4a895a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dissolveMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: ab5c1ffe75215bb499494022794ee36d, type: 2}
  animator: {fileID: 214206423}
  endButton: {fileID: 1008150034}
  endings:
  - name: 6
    endingLines:
    - They hauled Anthony away, the whole time screaming he didn't do it.
    - The family thanks you for your help, and you accept their praise with a smile.
      It all makes sense, it was a crime of passion, a crime of greed.
    - However, when you get home that night, one thought can't escape your mind..
    - '""Did I miss something?..." I guess you''ll never know'
  - name: 5
    endingLines:
    - As Natasha is read her rights, you're met with praises from the family. "You've
      done it again!"
    - As they take her away, you can't help but listen to her please and tears
    - It makes sense, it was a crime of self-preservation.
    - However, this case never sits right with you... but you couldn't have made
      a mistake, right?
  - name: 7
    endingLines:
    - As Jonathan is handcuffed, a sense if pride washes over you.
    - 'It was so simple, but hidden away so deeply. It was a crime of jealousy and
      self-preservation. '
    - The family thanks you and all that you have done.
    - And as you head home, you know you have your man.
  texts:
  - {fileID: 492379251}
  - {fileID: 1973740628}
  - {fileID: 1992466888}
  - {fileID: 2135007273}
